    "## 2. Création des nouvelles features\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 Ratios bytes\n",
    "\n",
    "Un ratio bytes source/destination très asymétrique peut indiquer une exfiltration de données ou un scan.  \n",
    "On utilise des opérations NumPy vectorisées — pas de boucles Python."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
<<<<<<< HEAD
   "execution_count": 5,
=======
   "execution_count": 3,
>>>>>>> e6ce9d0872e163a69c0ca60ee5c2951a91710736
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Ratios bytes créés : bytes_ratio, bytes_total, bytes_diff_norm\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "new_features = []  # on garde la liste de toutes les nouvelles features\n",
    "\n",
    "for df in [X_train, X_test]:\n",
    "    if 'sbytes' in df.columns and 'dbytes' in df.columns:\n",
    "        sb = df['sbytes'].values.astype(np.float32)\n",
    "        db = df['dbytes'].values.astype(np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "        df['bytes_ratio']     = sb / (db + 1)                        # asymétrie src/dst\n",
    "        df['bytes_total']     = sb + db                               # volume total\n",
    "        df['bytes_diff_norm'] = np.abs(sb - db) / (sb + db + 1)      # différence normalisée\n",
    "\n",
    "new_features += ['bytes_ratio', 'bytes_total', 'bytes_diff_norm']\n",
    "print(f'Ratios bytes créés : bytes_ratio, bytes_total, bytes_diff_norm')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.2 Ratios paquets\n",
    "\n",
    "Un scan réseau envoie beaucoup de paquets sans recevoir de réponse → ratio spkts/dpkts élevé."
   ]
  },
  {
